    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §47, Chap 2 of 1998",
    "lawSection": "Public Health",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6485\n\nSPONSOR: RIVERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 2 of the laws of 1998, amend-\ning the public health law and other laws relating to expanding the child\nhealth insurance plan, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo extend provisions of Child Health Plus related to presumptive eligi-\nbility, preventing fraud, and establishing premiums.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would extend the sunset provisions of chapter 2 of the laws of\n1998 for an additional two years, to expire July 1, 2021. The provisions\nbeing extended establish premiums under Child Health Plus. The bill\nwould also extend presumptive eligibility protections for children in\nthe program.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChild Health Plus provides a full-range of essential health care\nservices for youth across the state including diagnostic testing, treat-\nments, emergency services, and prescription and nonprescription drug\ncoverage. This legislation ensures that the current Child Health Plus\nprogram continues to operate effectively and provide affordable health\ncoverage to children.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n  New Legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n  None noted.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n  Immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
